  "text": "In August 2020, we returned again and again to the postal service. Thirty-three of us said \"the postal service\" on August 22; thirty of us said \"united states postal\" the same day, twenty-nine \"united states postal service,\" twenty-nine \"the united states postal,\" twenty-eight \"the united states postal service.\" The phrase had first appeared in our record on 2013-01-15, from John Hoeven. Twenty-three of us said \"the cares act.\" Twenty-two of us said \"delivering for america act,\" a phrase that entered our record on 2020-08-12. And on August 13, twenty-one of us said \"the united arab emirates,\" first said among us on 2015-02-05. That is what we converged on this month: the mail, and one foreign state. We report it as we said it.",
